{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"282c3e8d-1322-47d6-8022-e876afdcd7dc","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Torque measures a force’s turning effect. Here, a ten-newton upward force acts forty centimeters from a fixed pivot.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Torque: turning effect"},{"op":"figure","id":"lever","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.08,0.54],"y":[-0.12,0.34],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"bar","from":[0,0],"to":[0.4,0]},{"kind":"point","id":"pivot","at":[0,0],"label":"pivot"},{"kind":"point","id":"tip","at":[0.4,0]},{"kind":"segment","id":"force","from":{"at":"tip"},"to":[0.4,0.26],"arrow":true,"label":"10 N"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"282c3e8d-1322-47d6-8022-e876afdcd7dc","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The lever arm is the perpendicular distance from the pivot to the force’s line of action—not necessarily the bar’s length.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"distance","on":"lever","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"action","from":[0.4,-0.1],"to":[0.4,0.3],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"measure","from":[0,-0.065],"to":[0.4,-0.065],"label":"0.40 m"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"tip"},"from":[0.4,0.15],"to":{"at":"pivot"},"r":0.045}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\tau = Fd_{\\perp}"},{"op":"text","id":"definition","anchor":{"el":"rule","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Lever arm = perpendicular distance"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"282c3e8d-1322-47d6-8022-e876afdcd7dc","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Multiply force by the perpendicular lever arm: four newton-meters, counterclockwise. A force directed along the bar would have zero lever arm.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"turn","on":"lever","marks":[{"kind":"arc","center":{"at":"pivot"},"r":0.1,"start":10,"end":105,"arrow":true},{"kind":"text","at":[0.13,0.16],"text":"4 N·m","size":"normal"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"definition","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\tau=(10\\,\\mathrm{N})(0.40\\,\\mathrm{m})=4.0\\,\\mathrm{N\\,m}"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"If the same upward force acts halfway along the bar, what happens to the torque?","expected_gist":"It halves to 2 N·m because the lever arm halves."}}}
